# Books clean — definition of done

This exists because agents claimed “clean / accurate” books while Balance Sheet Net Income still disagreed with P&L (unclosed prior-year income left in revenue accounts).

## Never say “clean”, “accurate BS”, “fresh open”, or “closed” until ALL pass live

Run (or equivalent API checks) and quote results:

```bash
node scripts/verify-books-clean.mjs --entity ent-ljc --asOf YYYY-MM-DD
```

| # | Gate | Pass only if |
|---|------|----------------|
| 1 | Trial balance | `isBalanced === true` |
| 2 | Balance sheet equation | Assets − (L+E) = **$0.00** |
| 3 | Net Income tie-out | BS Net Income **equals** P&L for calendar YTD (Jan 1 .. asOf) |
| 4 | Prior-year P&L | No open revenue/expense residual before Jan 1 of asOf year |
| 5 | Plug/rollup accounts | 1999, 2999, 3020, 3900, 3995, 1100, 1020, 1021 all **$0** |
| 6 | Period integrity | `isClosed: true` only when claiming closed; else quote `canClose` + `blockers` |
| 7 | Cash/cards (if month in scope) | Monitored recons $0.00 difference / statement-tied |

## Forbidden shortcuts

- “TB balances” alone
- “Plugs are zero” alone
- “Cash reconciles” alone
- Integrity `databasePeriodStatus: CLOSED` without `isClosed: true`
- Chat memory of a prior close

## When you miss a gate

1. Fix the books (or the report) — do not argue immateriality
2. Encode the miss: integrity blocker, rule, or verify-script check so the next agent cannot skip it
3. Learning lives in **repo + API gates**, not in this chat
